# Lever 4's timed question: how much of gemm_iq2xxs's step time does the load-time plane + cp.async
# staging remove? The ncu read (2026-10-17, card l4-iq2xxs-ncu, A6000, arm gemm_iq2xxs_bolt_up_t448)
# decided the bind: dram/launch 351 MB = the once-set (ratio 1.02, DRAM 28 % SOL) — bytes already
# minimal; the bind is the weight path's instruction stream (~18 scalar warp-broadcast global loads +
# GRID2XXS lookups a warp-step; Compute 72 %, IMMA 7.1 %, LSU 38.3 %, L1TEX 55.1 %; stalls wait 17.5 /
# not_selected 16.2 / math_pipe_throttle 16.2 / long_scoreboard 10.8). The plane makes every row's
# half a 16-byte run (load-time repack, byte-neutral), so the weight words stage through
# cp.async into shared and the warps read v4 — the Q4_K path's shape.
#
# Site decomposition (lead, perf s2330/s2334, A6000 P=4096 eager): gemm_iq2xxs = ~532 ms weight
# re-read across passes (53.2 ms/pass) + ~286 ms compute at m=448 — the 0.80 s site of the 26.9 %
# share. The ubatch track owns the re-read's elimination; this card claims the compute part only
# (bytes are the file's, so the re-read's byte share does not move with the plane) and reports the
# per-pass re-read SPEED beside it as a second, unclaimed effect.
#
# Runner (from the integrated head after the engine flip, not this branch's inert tree):
#   just time-gpu-gemm gemm_iq2xxs_bolt_up_t448        # the arm, file entry vs plane entry
#   and the pp4096 A/B in the lead's sitting (ab-decode / depth-gpu prose:4096), both cards.
# Wall [derived]: arm ~2 min a side under the lease; the sitting's own window prices its rows.
kind: ab
question: Does the IQ2_XXS plane (staged weight words) cut the gemm_iq2xxs arm's compute time at Bolt's routed-up shape, and by how much of its ~81.8 ms/pass (53.2 re-read + 28.6 compute)?
term: the bench arm's per-launch time (file entry vs plane entry, interleaved), and the pp4096 pass delta both cards
unit: %
predict: -14..-10
rounds: 4
sd: 0.6 % AGENTS.md 「Know the ruler」 (same-binary run scatter); the compute leg is 28.6 ms of the
  arm's 81.8 ms/pass, so the pass row moves -0.08..-0.12 s of its ~2.97 s = -2.8..-3.9 % under the
  same ruler — the re-read leg's movement, if any, is reported beside it, never claimed here
condition: the arm at 432x2560x1024 top-9 t=448 grid 9900 on the A6000 under the machine lease, interleaved rounds, both entries byte-neutral over the same synthetic stack; the pass rows carry their card and depth
decide-in: the compute leg 1.4-1.7x (28.6 -> ~17-20 ms a pass, the arm -10..-14 %); the per-pass re-read 53.2 ms reported beside it, claimed only if it also clears 1.2x (DRAM 28 % SOL says the re-read is instruction-bound too, not bandwidth-bound)
decide-below: the compute leg under 1.2x — the weight-path instruction term was not the bind at the launch level; profile the plane entry once before any second step
decide-above: the arm past -20 % or the pass past -0.16 s — the re-read leg moved with it: report the split, keep the claim at the compute leg (the re-read's disappearance is the ubatch track's, not this plane's)
